                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm unable to understand how json::parse can create a vector containing PostCodeHandler objects."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/post_code.cpp",
                    "line": 127,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Min, I have added the helpers from_json(..., PostCodeHandler& handler) in line 68. This allows us to parse the PostCodeHandler. nlohmann can then just go from there since it can expand it to standard structures of that. See https://stackoverflow.com/questions/61708244/nlohmann-json-converting-to-and-from-nested-structures"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/post_code.cpp",
                    "line": 127,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for your detailed explanation. The resources you shared have been incredibly helpful in deepening my understanding of JSON."
                }
            ],
